# QUIL_SURFACE_STUB_V1

**Status:** Active — Post-3-Pass Scan  
**Purpose:** Allocate Quil surface identity and shell lifecycle matching the Linen control pattern.  
**Scope:** `servers/silk-shell/src/main.rs` only. No kernel/ABI/sexdisplay changes.  
**Reference:** `rapid/PHASE_05_QUIL_LANGUAGE_WORKSTATION.md` (full plan for Quil language workstation)

---

## Current State (commit 98cadaf)

Quil (`surface_id=201`) is a first-class shell-managed app surface, following the identical pattern established by Linen (`surface_id=200`). No Quil server binary exists — this is pure shell surface/frame integration.

### Surface Identity

| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| `SURFACE_ID_QUIL` | `201` |
| `QUIL_FRAME_ID` | `3` (frame 1 = APP/STATUS, frame 2 = Linen) |
| Boot geometry | `(100, 100, 640, 480)` |
| Frame flags | `FRAME_FLAG_TOP_BAR` (matching default) |
| Surface lifecycle | Always alive (`surface_is_alive(201) = true`), not destroyable |

### Wiring Changes (12 locations, 96cadaf)

| Location | Change |
|----------|--------|
| `SURFACE_ID_QUIL` constant (line 61) | Added next to `SURFACE_ID_LINEN` |
| Surface ID registry comment (line 77) | Added `201 quil (editor stub)` |
| `SURFACE_201_X/Y/W/H` statics (lines 997-1000) | Geometry tracking |
| `tile_visible_frames()` (line 698) | QUIL match arm for tiling position |
| `emit_snapshot()` (line 1053) | QUIL `OP_SURFACE_UPDATE` for position sync |
| `get_surface_bounds()` (line 1068) | QUIL returns geometry |
| `point_in_surface()` (line 1090) | QUIL bounds check |
| `surface_is_alive()` (line 1118) | Returns `true` always (like Linen) |
| `is_focusable_surface()` (line 1209) | QUIL is focusable |
| `is_closeable_surface()` (line 1933) | QUIL cannot be closed (OS-managed) |
| `update_local_geometry()` (line 698) | QUIL geometry sync |
| `z_order` arrays (line 1167, 2977) | QUIL in focus fallback order |

### New Helpers (5, matching Linen pattern)

| Helper | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| `ensure_quil_frame()` | Creates `ShellFrame` with `frame_id=3` lazily. Returns `Some(3)` or `None`. |
| `open_quil_in_active_scene()` | Opens Quil in current scene (un-minimize, 0xEC, tile, focus). |
| `focus_or_open_quil()` | Focus if visible, else open. |
| `toggle_quil()` | Toggle minimize/restore. |
| `quil_frame_id()` | Returns `Some(3)` or `None`. |

All helpers are lazy — Quil only enters `FRAMES` on first open. Zero boot visual change.

---

## Exact Invariants

### Surface Lifecycle
- `surface_is_alive(201)` returns `true` always (hardcoded, never changes)
- Quil cannot be tombstoned (`is_tombstoned` never set for 201)
- `is_closeable_surface(201)` returns `false`
- `is_focusable_surface(201)` returns `true`
- No `SURFACE_201_ALIVE` static exists (unlike surfaces 100-103)

### Frame Lifecycle
- Frame `frame_id=3` created lazily on first `ensure_quil_frame()` call
- Frame created in first empty FRAMES slot (0..3)
- Scene assigned to `ACTIVE_SCENE_IDX` on creation and on every `open_quil_in_active_scene()` call
- Frame persists until overwritten (no destroy path in V1)
- Frame uses `FRAME_FLAG_TOP_BAR` (matching default frame style)

### Tab Lifecycle
- Single tab per frame (1:1:1 frame:tab:surface model, matching V1 constraint)
- Tab `surface_id=201`, `title_id=0`, `flags=0`
- Tab count always 1, active tab always 0
- No close/destroy path for tab (Quil is OS-managed)

### Scene Behavior
- Quil frame starts in `ACTIVE_SCENE_IDX` when created
- `open_quil_in_active_scene()` reassigns frame to current scene
- `sync_scene_visibility()` shows/hides Quil based on frame's scene_id
- Before frame exists: Quil not affected by scene switches (no frame to check)

### Snapshot Behavior
- Quil frame captured by `snap_capture_layout()` (iterates FRAMES)
- `snap_restore_layout()` includes Quil if frame exists
- `surface_is_alive(201)=true` means snap_restore always considers Quil alive
- No tombstone check for Quil (never tombstoned)

