## Known Imperfections (3-Pass Scan Results)

### PASS 1 — Correctness / Integration

| # | Severity | Issue | Location | Details |
|---|----------|-------|----------|---------|
| 1 | **Critical** | `clear_focus_if_dead()` can focus non-existent Quil | Lines 1167-1176 | When a surface is closed, z_order fallback tries QUIL first. `surface_is_alive(201)=true` + `surface_in_active_scene(201)` returns true via fallback (surface not in any frame → treated as panel) → `try_set_focus(201)` succeeds even without frame. Keyboard input goes nowhere. **Same bug pre-existing for Linen.** |
| 2 | **Medium** | Hit-test z_order missing QUIL | Line 2977 | Focus-fallback z_order (line 1167) includes QUIL first. Hit-test z_order (line 2977) skips QUIL entirely. Clicking Quil area while another surface focused won't register. |
| 3 | **Low** | `close_surface_from_frame_light` hardcoded for 100-103 | Lines 1949-1954 | Uses `match` with explicit surface IDs. Adding new closeable surface requires updating this match. Currently safe because `is_closeable_surface` gates all callers, but latent fragility. |

### PASS 2 — Architecture / Boundary

| # | Severity | Issue | Location | Details |
|---|----------|-------|----------|---------|
| 4 | **Medium** | Linen/Quil helper duplication | Lines 1529-1864 | ~140 lines of near-identical code. Should be parameterized in V2 as `ensure_app_frame(frame_id, surface_id, geometry)`. |
| 5 | **Low** | Surface ID registry is a comment, not enforced | Lines 68-77 | No compile-time/runtime check prevents overlapping surface IDs. |
| 6 | **Medium** | Split ownership of surface lifecycle | Throughout | Shell manages frame lifecycle but Linen server creates its own surface independently. Quil has no server yet but shell already manages its lifecycle. Server could create surface at different coordinates. |
| 7 | **Low** | Magic ID coupling in 12+ shell locations | Throughout | Surface ID 201 hardcoded in 12 locations. If ID changes, all must update. No enum/registry. |
| 8 | **Low** | FRAMES array size constraint (4 max) | Throughout | MAX_FRAMES=4, 3 allocated (APP, Linen, Quil). Only 1 slot for all future frame-based apps. |
| 9 | **Low** | No dynamic surface registration protocol | N/A | All surfaces defined at compile-time. No runtime registration for new servers. |
| 10 | **Low** | z_order inconsistency between arrays | Lines 1167 vs 2977 | Focus-fallback: `[QUIL, LINEN, TEST4, TEST3, STATIC, APP]`. Hit-test: `[LINEN, TEST4, TEST3, STATIC, APP]`. Missing QUIL + different priority. |

### PASS 3 — Product / Future-Proof

| # | Severity | Issue | Location | Details |
|---|----------|-------|----------|---------|
| 11 | **High** | No keyboard binding for Quil | Lines 468-573 | No `Focus201` SurfaceAction variant. No scancode for opening Quil. `FocusToggle` cycle excludes Quil. User cannot open Quil. |
| 12 | **Medium** | No visual placeholder | N/A | Opening Quil (0xEC on surface 201) with no server produces blank/black area. No "coming soon" indicator. |
| 13 | **Low** | Weak V1 success criteria | QUIL_SURFACE_STUB_V1.md | No checklist for "stub ready". No acceptance criteria. |
| 14 | **Low** | No runtime marker naming canon | Lines 1743-1803 | Uses `[shell.quil.*]` but no documented convention. Risk of inconsistent markers. |
| 15 | **Low** | No rollback plan | N/A | If surface ID 201 conflicts with future server, no documented migration path. |
| 16 | **Low** | Handoff docs don't document known bugs | QUIL_SURFACE_STUB_V1.md | Focus-fallback bug (PASS 1 #1) and hit-test z_order issue (PASS 1 #2) not documented. |
| 17 | **Low** | Single surface ID for multi-panel Quil | Line 61 | PHASE_05 plan envisions 4-panel layout (tree, canvas, inspector, console). Only 1 surface ID allocated. Future phases need surface allocation strategy. |

