## V2 Boundaries (servers/quil)

When `servers/quil/src/main.rs` is created, it will:

1. Create surface 201 via 0xEC on launch (using its PDX slot to sexdisplay)
2. Receive keyboard input via OP_HID_EVENT forwarded from silk-shell
3. Render colored rectangles for typed characters (no glyph pipeline)
4. Implement Text Mode first, then Sex Mode PDX graph overlay

The shell-side stub prepared in V1 handles:
- Surface identity (201) and frame slot (frame 3)
- Scene-aware visibility (show/hide on workspace switch)
- Minimize/restore/zoom via standard frame operations
- Layout snapshot persistence (in-memory)
- Focus ordering (z_order, FocusToggle cycle pending keyboard binding)

### V2 Registration Protocol (Suggested)

When Quil server boots:
1. Quil creates surface 201 via 0xEC (standard PDX pattern)
2. Shell detects surface already has frame (from V1 stub) → no extra setup needed
3. Shell forwards keyboard input to Quil's surface ID
4. Quil renders on surface 201

If no Quil frame exists (fresh boot without V1 stub), shell creates one on first 0xEC from surface 201.

---

## Non-Goals (V1 Stub)

- Not a Quil server binary (`servers/quil/`)
- No keyboard input routing to Quil surface
- No text/code/sex mode implementations
- No Sex Inspector panels
- No project tree via Linen
- No visual placeholder/rendering on surface 201 (no server)
- No dynamic surface registration protocol
- No FRAMES array expansion (stays at 4)
- No z_order priority optimization
- No helper deduplication/parameterization

