## Handoff Warnings

1. **Focus fallback targets non-existent Quil** — `clear_focus_if_dead()` at line 1167 tries QUIL first in z_order. Since `surface_is_alive(201)=true` and `surface_in_active_scene(201)` returns true via fallback (surface not in any frame → treated as panel), `try_set_focus(201)` succeeds even without a Quil frame. After closing any surface, focus "disappears" into surface 201. Fix: add `frame_for_surface(sid).is_some()` guard in z_order loop. Pre-existing for Linen (surface 200).

2. **Hit-test z_order missing QUIL** — Line 2977 hit-test array excludes `SURFACE_ID_QUIL`. Click-to-focus on Quil area broken when another surface is focused.

3. **No keyboard binding** — No scancode opens Quil. `FocusToggle` cycle (line 3884) skips Quil entirely. Must add `Focus201` SurfaceAction variant and binding before Quil is user-accessible.

4. **Linen has same bugs** — Both PASS 1 #1 and #2 affect Linen identically. Fix both surfaces at once.

5. **`surface_in_active_scene()` fallback is wrong for frame-owned surfaces** — Line 1227 returns `true` for any surface not found in FRAMES. Works for panels/cursor (always visible) but wrong for Linen/Quil (frame-owned, should return false if no frame). This is the root cause of PASS 1 #1.

6. **Two z_order arrays must remain in sync** — Line 1167 (focus fallback) and line 2977 (hit-test). Currently inconsistent. Keep updated together.

